    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d317">

                <pb facs="0359" n="351" xml:id="pg351"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.001 Selassie I/370: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the Emperor of Ethiopia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Haile Selassie I</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-20">May 20, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have received Your Majesty’s message informing me of your return to Addis
                    Ababa, and I assure you of the satisfaction with which I have received these
                    tidings. On behalf of the people and Government of the United States I have
                    great pleasure in extending to Your Majesty my most sincere felicitations on
                    this notable occasion and my best wishes for Your Majesty’s health and
                    happiness.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin</hi> D. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Roosevelt</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
